[center][size=5][b]Start as Anyone[/b][/size]
[img]https://img.shields.io/badge/Bannerlord-1.4.7-blue.svg[/img] [img]https://img.shields.io/badge/Maintained-yes-green.svg[/img] ﻿﻿
[size=4][b]Description[/b][/size]
Ever wanted to play as Rhagaea, Derthert, Corein, or any other established character in Calradia? “Start as Anyone” makes this possible by allowing you to choose from the complete list of existing lords when starting a new game.[/center]
[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Start your campaign as [b]any existing lord[/b] in the game[/*]
[*]Inherit their clan, relations, and holdings[/*]
[*][b]Compatible[/b] with the base game and total overhaul mods like [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mountandblade2bannerlord/mods/2907]Realm Of Thrones[/url]﻿, [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mountandblade2bannerlord/mods/6723]Anno Domini 1259[/url] [/*]
[*]Fully compatible with major overhaul mods such as [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mountandblade2bannerlord/mods/7738]Victorian Era: 1860[/url]﻿[/*]
[*]Seamless integration with the game’s existing systems[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Mount & Blade II: Bannerlord 1.4.7 (for older game versions, use the matching older release of the mod)[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mountandblade2bannerlord/mods/2006]Harmony[/url] ([b]required[/b] dependency)[/*]
[*]Improved Minor Factions mod if you want to fully experience minor faction gameplay.[/*]
[/list]

[b][size=4]Partner Mods:[/size][/b]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mountandblade2bannerlord/mods/6771]Improved Minor Factions[/url][b] - [/b]Improved Minor Factions is a mod that aims to bring some life to the Minor Factions of Bannerlord by adding Minor Faction Hideouts that allow the player to recruit Minor faction troops and raid them as well as adding many new Quests. [b]Use this if you want to play as a minor faction hero.[/b]﻿[/*]
[/list]


[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[b]Step 1: Install Harmony[/b]
[list]
[*]Download the latest version of Harmony from [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mountandblade2bannerlord/mods/2006]Nexus Mods[/url][/*]
[*]Extract the contents of the Harmony zip file to your Bannerlord’s [i]Modules[/i] directory
[list]
[*] Typically located at: [i]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Mount & Blade II Bannerlord\Modules[/i][/*]
[*]Ensure you have a folder structure like: [i]Modules\Harmony\[/i][/*]
[/list]
[b]Step 2: Install Start as Anyone[/b]
[list]
[*] Download the latest release .zip file[/*]
[*]Extract the contents to your Bannerlord’s [i]Modules[/i] directory[/*]
[*]Ensure you have a folder structure like: [i]Modules\StartAsAnyone\[/i][/*]
[/list]
[b]Step 3: Loading Order[/b]
[list]
[*] Launch Mount & Blade II: Bannerlord[/*]
[*]Click on “Mods” from the main menu[/*]
[*]Ensure “Start as Anyone” is bottom of the loading order. Also have Harmony on.[/*]
[*]Click “Play”[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Usage[/b][/size]
[list]
[*] From the main menu, select “Sandbox” (Sandbox is recommended when playing as an existing character)[/*]
[*]In the character creation screen, you will see additional options to select from existing lords[/*]
[*]Choose your desired character and begin your adventure[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Known Issues[/b][/size]
[list]
[*] You must select difficulty settings after starting the game, from the campaign options menu[/*]
[*]Some quest or storyline elements might be affected when playing as existing characters[/*]
[*]Special clan abilities or unique features may behave unexpectedly in certain situations[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Compatibility
[/b][/size]   This mod has been tested with:
[list]
[*] Bannerlord version 1.4.7[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Support[/b][/size]If you encounter any issues or have suggestions, please:
[list]
[*] Check the [b]Known Issues[/b] section[/*]
[*]Submit an issue on the [url=https://github.com/kerema14/StartAsAnyone/issues]GitHub Issues[/url] page[/*]
[/list]
